# S1b: the four-card sibling DMA kernels against the pinned pair kernels at the PAIR's page counts, on one card (QWEN_FAST_TP
# unset, TP4_WIDTH=2). A failure means a sibling changed what the pair does: stop, nothing at four cards means anything then.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives
# the window (the graft directory and the graft binary digest of the one-card harnesses); every other value is final.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image S0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Under the watcher: this is the first hardware launch of the _tp sibling DMA kernels, so an out-of-range DMA is a named error,
# not a hang that costs a reset. Duration (estimate): 10-25 min. Also the first run of the gdn_tp4 harness's import path inside the harness image (the image's own
# PYTHONPATH entries stay behind /bench/ci), so a plumbing fault shows here, cheaply.
# Read the GDN_TP4 verdict line for section PARITY: PASS, every kernel byte-equal.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections PARITY
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=gdn_tp4 TP4_WIDTH=2 WATCHER=1 KOPGRAFT64=/home/thatch/opgraft-K64j EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=152951c1c0de5c9dfad2d62c295393a43b2ecf353965c55c709da7e539b975b7
